From: rocjitsu vfio-user development
Subject: [PATCH] amdgpu: replace BUG() with pr_warn_once in invalid_rreg for vfio-user probe

When rocjitsu exposes a virtual GFX950 GPU via libvfio-user, the amdgpu
driver probes it via the CHIP_IP_DISCOVERY path. During
amdgpu_discovery_set_ip_blocks(), the driver calls RREG32(0x16061)
(mmMP0_SMN_C2PMSG_33) to poll for firmware-ready. That register address
(0x16061 * 4 = 0x58184) exceeds the direct BAR5 window (256 KB), so
amdgpu_device_rreg() routes it through adev->pcie_rreg, which is not
yet initialized at this point in probe. The result is a call to
amdgpu_invalid_rreg() which hits BUG() and crashes the kernel.

Replace BUG() with pr_warn_once() + return 0 so the driver survives the
unimplemented register access. The C2PMSG_33 polling loop in
amdgpu_discovery_read_binary_from_mem() proceeds after exhausting its
1000 iterations with value 0 (bit 31 never set), then correctly reads
mmRCC_CONFIG_MEMSIZE (0xde3 * 4 = 0x378C, within BAR5) which returns
the VRAM size in MB, and locates the IP discovery binary in VRAM.

The rocjitsu BAR5 model (bar5_mmio.cpp) returns 256 for
mmRCC_CONFIG_MEMSIZE, so the driver reads the discovery table from VRAM
at offset (256 MB - DISCOVERY_TMR_OFFSET). The discovery table is
written by Bar0Vram into the VRAM memfd at construction time.

A companion fix in amd/amdgpu/Makefile adds -Wno-unused-variable to
suppress a pre-existing warning (dev_attr_pcie_replay_count) that the
DKMS build treats as -Werror.

This patch is intended for the amdgpu-dkms package used with rocjitsu
vfio-user GPU emulation. It is not appropriate for upstream submission
as-is; the correct long-term fix is to initialize pcie_rreg before
ip_discovery runs, or to stub C2PMSG_33 via the NBIO IP block.

Applies to: amdgpu-dkms 6.12.12-2147987.24.04 (ROCm 6.4), 6.19.4-2337710.24.04 (ROCm 6.4+)
Tested on:  kernel 6.8.0-134-generic, 6.17.0-35-generic, Ubuntu 24.04 Noble

Note: The Makefile -Wno-unused-variable fix is applied separately via sed
in rebuild-and-reload.sh because the Makefile header varies across versions.

--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
@@ -1270,10 +1270,12 @@ static uint32_t amdgpu_invalid_rreg(struct amdgpu_device *adev, uint32_t reg)
 {
-	DRM_ERROR("Invalid callback to read register 0x%04X\n", reg);
-	BUG();
-	return 0;
+	/* rocjitsu-vfu: pcie_rreg may be uninitialized during ip_discovery probe.
+	 * pr_warn instead of BUG so the driver survives unimplemented register
+	 * accesses (e.g. mmMP0_SMN_C2PMSG_33 = 0x16061) and falls through to
+	 * read RCC_CONFIG_MEMSIZE from direct BAR5 to locate the IP discovery
+	 * table in VRAM. */
+	pr_warn_once("amdgpu: rreg 0x%04X via unset pcie_rreg\n", reg);
+	return 0;
 }

